kniga-alhimika-name = alchemist's book
kniga-alhimika-desc = A massive volume bound in scaly leather, scorched in places and splashed with hardened drops of multicolored mixtures. The pages give off a sharp smell of sulfur and dried wormwood.
kniga-alhimika-content = [head=3]Observation Journal of Lurtz-Idu[/head]


    {"[italic]The sssun bakes the ssscales... Sssand gets under the clawsss.[/italic]"}


    {"That warm-blooded Mahmud came again. Too much noise, too much waving of handsss. Brought flatbreadsss and that sssour water they call milk. A lizard's stomach does not like such giftsss, but Lurtz-Idu knowsss: good relations bring gold. I will use it as a bassse for a caustic solvent."}


    {"[bold]Order report:[/bold]"}

    {"Blue potion on cactusss extract and crushed scarab beetle shell worked as intended. The camel's swelling went down. Recorded proportionsss: three partsss juice, one part poison, stir slowly until emerald vapor appearsss. A fine vapor it wasss, thick."}


    {"[bold]Current tasksss:[/bold]"}

    {"- Sssand has blown into the shop again. Must repair the threshold, or sssoon Lurtz-Idu will be brewing nothing but dusty stormsss."}

    {"- Cheese on the counter is excellent bait for desssert ratsss. I need their spleensss for speed potionsss. Most important: do not eat the bait myssself. It sssmells far too tempting."}

    {"- Let the web in the corner hang. Spider sssnare fliesss, and fliesss disturb thinking."}


    {"[italic]Evening note:[/italic]"}

    {"Must test how fire sssalt reacts with ssserpent bile. If it flares again, Lurtz-Idu will have to ssseek a new table. Again."}


    {"- Lurtz-Idu"}

bortovoy-zhurnal-galery-name = galley's logbook
bortovoy-zhurnal-galery-desc = A thick leather-bound book blackened by salt and damp worked deep into it. The Legion's crest is embossed on the cover, and the pages within are filled with an officer's strict, cramped hand. The final lines were written in obvious haste, the ink smeared.
bortovoy-zhurnal-galery-content = [head=3]Daily Journal of the Galley "Unyielding"[/head]


    {"10th day of the Harvest month."}

    {"We weighed anchor at the second glass of the morning watch. Sea calm, wind north-east, sailing on a quartering wind. Escorting transports with provisions and powder draught to the besieged fortress. The rowers at the benches pull most commendably. The crew's spirit is sound. Glory to the Legion."}


    {"14th day of the Harvest month."}

    {"Sea battle abeam the cape. Two thief-vessels sprang from behind the shoal and attempted to gain the weather gauge. Raised the alarm, all hands above! Fired a cruel blast of grapeshot from the bow chasers. The gunners know their work: one rebel galley was sent to feed the fish. Yet the enemy answered with tremendous fire, cannonballs falling like hail, as though their powder magazines were bottomless. Took a ball to port. Bulwark pierced, running rigging damaged, yet the spars remain whole."}


    {"19th day of the Harvest month."}

    {"The sea is greatly troubled, waves striking the bow. We hold the blockade of the bay, lying adrift under storm canvas. Among the sailors forward there has begun vile talk and unrest. They claim that the rebels' guns and shot are supplied by a bony dead man, that is to say, port undead. To halt whining and panic, I ordered two topmen thrashed mercilessly with rope ends on the quarterdeck before the formation. The Legion does not believe in such old wives' tales."}


    {"24th day of the Harvest month."}

    {"The dog watch proved bloody. Thief-galleys emerged from the fog directly ahead, showing no lights. The enemy fires to kill and spares no powder draught. We lost two guns on the port side, and eighteen men of the boarding party were gutted by cannon fire. Took a breach below the waterline. The bilge crew have not left the pumps, bailing without cease."}


    {"In vain we tried to row into clear water. The draft increased greatly from the incoming water, and in the thick fog we were carried off the fairway. We struck a stone bank with a terrible crack, the keel broken in two, the bottom torn open. The galley is dying. Gave the final order: lower the boats and abandon ship. What an inglorious, most shameful end for the proud pennant of the Legion. True disgrace and dishonor upon my head."}

zalyapannyy-kizyakom-dnevnik-name = dung-smeared diary
zalyapannyy-kizyakom-dnevnik-desc = Several sheets of coarse paper stitched with harsh thread, covered in brown stains and dried crusts of manure. The little book reeks unbearably of heat, dust, and livestock, and the text is scratched with something sharp and filthy.
zalyapannyy-kizyakom-dnevnik-content = [head=3][color=#a0522d]Farid's Notes[/color][/head]


    {"[italic]At the start of the Month of Yellow Winds[/italic]"}

    {"Sun burns, damn it all. My back burns like an old tandoor. My donkey has become a stubborn bastard, will not walk, only spits. Today the Shah's guards came. Sabers shining, faces fat. Took the last skinny ram. Wife howls, old fool, kicking sand. Guards said the great Shah awaits a guest from the north, Jarl Otto Stark is coming. Why in hell do we need that snow bastard Otto? Let him gnaw ice at home. And because of his visit, now I chew dry dung."}


    {"[italic]Right after the great storm[/italic]"}

    {"May shaitan tear me apart! Five days eating nothing but sand and dead locust. My donkey, flea-bitten wretch, ate my right sandal from hunger. Palace is feasting, drums beating so hard the roof sheds dust. Bazaar folk say this Otto Stark drank a bucket of wine and did not even vomit. Strong dzhigit, curse him by the leg! Shah hugged him, called him blood brother. And here we swell from hunger. If donkey eats left sandal, by the sands, I will spill his guts and make strings for a dutar."}


    {"[italic]When the moon became a crooked saber[/italic]"}

    {"The icy bastard Stark left. Loaded our gold onto his wagons and vanished. Shah now walks proud: we are brothers with northerners, he says, we stand back to back! Ah, what joy, damn it root and branch! Brother left, and tax collector is right here. Says pay new tax, guest ate much, treasury empty. Took the last sack of flour. Now I sit bare, in one sandal. Donkey looks at me and laughs. May mountain trolls love you all in the backside."}

mogila-kakogo-to-dvorfa-name = grave of some dwarf

skomkannyy-chernovik-name = crumpled draft
skomkannyy-chernovik-desc = A wrinkled piece of silk paper smelling of cheap incense. The sheet has been folded and crushed more than once, fraying the gold fringe along the edges. The text is written broadly, with smudges from a hurried hand in places.
skomkannyy-chernovik-content = [head=3][color=#b8860b]Message from Shah Ali Ibn-Taram[/color][/head]


    {"[italic]Hey, respected Jarl Otto Stark! Shah Ali Ibn-Taram sends you salaam!"}


    {"Listen, dear, I hear many good rumor about you. They say you are strong man, true dzhigit, even if you live in your cold snow. I respect your axe and your courage."}


    {"I think here, why we be just stranger people? You strong ruler, I strong ruler. Let us become blood brothers, yes! We cut hand with knife, speak oath. Together stand back to back, any enemy we shake by the pipe!"}


    {"Come to my land, Jarl Otto! Do not sit where ice is. My tent is your tent. I will cut fattest fat-tailed ram for you, pour sweet wine. We sit on silk carpet and speak like respected people."}


    {"[color=#555555]██████████▓▓▓▒▒▒░░░[/color]"}

    {"[color=#555555]██████▓▓▓▒▒▒▒▒░░░[/color]"}

    {"[color=#555555]██████▓▓▓▓▓▒▒▒░░░[/color]"}


    {"[color=#555555]██████▓▓▓▒▒▒░░░░░[/color]"}

    {"[color=#555555]██████▓▓▓▓▓▓▒▒▒░░░[/color]"}


    {"I wait your answer, dear. Come as guest, leave as true brother!"}


    {"[bold]- Shah Ali Ibn-Taram[/bold][/italic]"}

ispachkannyy-spetsiyami-list1-name = spice-stained sheet
ispachkannyy-spetsiyami-list1-desc = The sheet is badly crumpled, with the distinct yellow stains of saffron. The text is written in a broad merchant's hand, with letters blurred in places as though tea had been spilled on the paper.
ispachkannyy-spetsiyami-list1-content = On the first day after crossing the dunes

    {"Reached the settlement, damn it all. Sand everywhere, in ears, in boots, even crunches in the food. Camels barely drag their legs, humped bastards, always begging water. This village is a hole of holes, but Shah Ali Ibn-Taram, may the gods send him a bucket of shade, promised no one would touch us. Said: come in, dear, rest! Only his guards at the entrance immediately took two bales of silk \"for the court's needs\". Listen, this is not tax, this is robbery in broad daylight, may shaitan take them!"}

smyatyy-pergament02-name = crumpled parchment
smyatyy-pergament02-desc = A dirty, rubbed sheet. The writing is crooked and blotted. The author clearly is not used to holding a quill often.
smyatyy-pergament02-content = Broke through the wall. Ate so much sand that we will be shitting bricks in the privy now. Mikula keeps whining about ghouls and fevers, while Klim is already pawing girls in the tavern for gold. Told them to shut their mouths and swing picks. The wise woman did not lie. It truly reeks of old sorcery here. Main thing is to find that golden tub with the djinn. We will wish for a sack of revents, buy our own tavern, and tell the elder to shove off.

nakaz-atamana-name = chieftain's order
nakaz-atamana-desc = A piece of rough parchment nailed with a crooked dagger to a wooden post in the middle of an abandoned desert camp. Written in broad strokes with a mixture of soot and camel blood.
nakaz-atamana-content = [head=3]Order of the Chieftain to the Brothers Left Behind[/head]


    {"Salaam, coyotes of the desert!"}


    {"If you are reading this message, your chieftain Kildibek and the best dzhigits are already rocking on the waves. Our sands have grown boring, yes? Thin caravans, little gold, only sand crunching between the teeth. Is that a life for true cutters?"}


    {"Clever people whispered that beyond the great blue water lie fat and wealthy lands. The peasants there are timid as sheep and throw nothing but manure with pitchforks. We sail there to take all of it under us! We will eat fresh meat, drink sweet wine, and sleep on strangers' featherbeds while the local swineherds wash our feet."}


    {"And you listen to the order, eh! Sit in camp, guard the wells. Do not gnaw each other's throats over small coin. Whoever starts trouble, I come back and shave his head with my axe myself! Once we settle firmly there and tear off the first fat prize, I will send boats for you."}


    {"Wait for word and sharpen your sabers! Soon we will milk those new lands together."}


    {"Chieftain Kildibek Ibn Nur-Kerimberdy."}

ispachkannyy-spetsiyami-list2-name = spice-stained sheet
ispachkannyy-spetsiyami-list2-content = Before departure

    {"That is it, we leave tomorrow at dawn before they render us down into tail fat. The settlement stinks, and not only of camels. It smells of trouble. Shah celebrates his \"brotherhood\", drums beating, and people's eyes are mean as hungry dogs. Listen, dear, my grandfather said: \"If a ruler kisses a foreigner, the poor man's trousers will soon be taken.\" So it happened. They set a tax so heavy the caravan is three sacks of gold lighter now. We turn toward the mountains. Better to trade with mountain trolls than these \"blood brothers\", damn them in both nostrils."}

pylnyy-pergament-name = dusty parchment
pylnyy-pergament-desc = A battered piece of coarse paper held to the table by a lump of dry yellow clay. The letters are crooked, the ink faded in the sun, but it is plainly written from the heart.
pylnyy-pergament-content = [head=3]Letter of Thanks to Wise Lurtz-Idu![/head]


    {"Hey, salaam, respected tailed lord! Sun to your house and cool shade to your shop! Mahmud from the southern tents writes to you. May your scales always shine like a new copper kazan, I swear by a hundred goats!"}


    {"Yesterday a shaitan-scorpion half the size of a dog stung my best camel, beautiful Zuhra. Her leg swelled like a ripe melon, Zuhra cries, I cry! Thought that was it, end of my trade, I go begging with a sack. Local healers only waved their hands, said: \"Ready the knife, Mahmud, cut her for meat.\""}


    {"But your blue bottle, the one you gave me for three miserable coppers... Ai, it is miracle-water! Smeared the wound, it hissed, black venom crawled out by itself like a frightened jerboa! In the morning I come out, Zuhra is already chewing dry thorns, spitting at me, happy!"}


    {"Thank you, wise lizard! Your potions are pure gold. You are not just an alchemist, you are my brother! My wife baked the sweetest flatbreads, and I prepared a jug of the best kumis. Tomorrow my youngest son will bring them to your shop. Live long, Lurtz-Idu-aga, may Allah grant you health!"}

akkuratno-slozhennyy-klochok-name = neatly folded scrap
akkuratno-slozhennyy-klochok-content = [italic]

    {"Rubbed it. Out came no naked woman and no kindly old man, but some mug of smoke and fire. Angry as a chained dog. Roared so loud my teeth hurt: \"One wish, and quickly!\""}


    {"I forgot everything from fright and blurted the first thing that came to mind: I want women to love me, I said, dote on me, take me for one of their own!"}


    {"The creature only snorted. Shot upward, smashed its head through the wall, and vanished, leaving only sand pouring from the hole."}


    {"And my beard fell out at once. I looked down, Mother of God, everything below my ears was bald, smooth as an egg! My voice squeaked, my shoulders shrank, and my filthy trousers went and turned into... a little dress. Right on me! With a white apron and lace, like a lord's maidservant."}


    {"Now I understand how women will love me. Braid my hair, dress me up, and share secrets. I tore off that shame and now sit naked on a stone, clutching the lace skirt in my hands and bawling in a thin little voice. I cannot go back to the village now. Our drunken villeins do not like jokes. I showed off once too often."}


    {"Janek."}

    {"[/italic]"}

zalyapannyy-list02-name = stained sheet
zalyapannyy-list02-desc = The parchment is crumpled, with fresh blood and dirt stains along the edges.
zalyapannyy-list02-content = Bloody sons of whores. We found the lamp. Shining on the stone like a tomcat's balls in the sun. I did not even get my mouth open before Klim yelled he would make the first wish. Mikula cracked him across the spine with a pick for it, and Klim opened Mikula's guts with a knife. Now both lie in the sand, bubbling blood. To hell with them, village fools. It is all mine now. I will rub this tin, and farewell pig tails and torn breeches.

ispachkannyy-spetsiyami-list3-name = spice-stained sheet
ispachkannyy-spetsiyami-list3-content = In the middle of trade week

    {"Listen, trade here is tight as an old boot. People's purses hold only dust and dead flies. Tried to sell mirrors, and they fear looking at their own faces, spit on them. Saw that Shah, sitting on silks, fat face, telling tales about northern Jarl Stark. Blood brother, he says! We embraced, he says! And all the while he eyes my spices like a hyena eyes carrion. After that \"brother\", seems only wind walks in the treasury. Local men wander like shadows, baring teeth. Saw one called Farid looking at his donkey as though it were made of pure meat. Bad sign, damn it. Time to carry my legs away."}

gryaznoe-pismo2-name = dirty letter
gryaznoe-pismo2-desc = The handwriting is broad and uncertain. Many words are spelled by ear, with bits of army bureaucracy scattered through it.
gryaznoe-pismo2-content = My lord father and my lady mother!


    {"Most humbly I bow my head and ask for your parental blessing. I report to you concerning myself, that to this date, by God's mercy, I am alive and well."}


    {"We stand in camp against the rebel fortress by the very ocean. Our commanders expected to bring those rebels quickly to obedience, but the thieves locked themselves in tight and fire their guns most cruelly. From the water, their galleys shoot without cease, causing us great distress and loss."}


    {"Our siege service, my lord father, is most necessary and laborious. We lead approaches and trenches toward their walls through great wet and clay. Cold winds blow from the ocean, the soldiers' greatcoats are very poor, and we sleep nearly in puddles under enemy bombs. Provisions are issued scantily, the hardtack has molded from damp, and the meat ration is wholly rotten. The other day we went to assault, but the enemy met us with grapeshot most cruelly, and many of ours were slain at the very gates."}


    {"Only you, mother, do not fall into grief and do not shed tears in vain. I do not climb forward needlessly in battles, and I keep my musket and powder dry. Since that fortress has little stores, soon they will wither, and we shall have full victory over them."}


    {"And when we break those thieves, they will give us pay, and I will certainly ask leave to visit you at our native yard. I promise to preserve my life."}


    {"I remain your most obedient and loving son."}

